<title>INDIA: India's 96/97 cotton crop seen at 16 mln bales.</title>
<headline>India's 96/97 cotton crop seen at 16 mln bales.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Cotton Advisory Board (CAB) on Monday estimated the 1996/97 (Oct-Sept) crop at 16 million bales (one bale is 170 kgs), the same as in the previous year.  </p>
<p>The Board had earlier estimated the crop size at 15.5 million bales at a meeting in December 1996.</p>
<p>CAB chairman B.C. Khatua said mid-winter rains had helped boost the cotton crop in southern, central and western India.</p>
<p>-- Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
